      "attempt": "United Internet AG is one of the leading internet service providers in Germany. Its Taxonomy-eligible turnover typically refers to revenues from services that fall under specific categories as defined by financial or industry standards. For United Internet, these services can include a variety of offerings within its portfolio, which primarily consist of internet access services, hosting services, cloud computing solutions, and other digital services.\n\nThe cloud and online services that contribute to United Internet's Taxonomy-eligible turnover include:\n\n1. **Internet Access Services**: This includes broadband internet services provided to residential and business customers.\n2. **Hosting Services**: United Internet offers various hosting solutions, including web hosting, email hosting, and dedicated server hosting.\n3. **Cloud Computing Solutions**: These include Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS), Platform as a Service (PaaS), and Software as a Service (SaaS) offerings. Examples might be cloud storage, virtual servers, and managed cloud environments.\n4. **Online Media Services**: Services like streaming platforms or content delivery networks could also be part of their revenue streams.\n5. **Managed Security Services**: Offering cybersecurity solutions and services to protect customer data and infrastructure.\n6. **Colocation Services**: Providing space for customers' own servers and networking equipment in United Internet’s data centers.\n\nEach of these services contributes to the overall revenue and, therefore, the Taxonomy-eligible turnover of United Internet. The exact breakdown would depend on the specific financial reporting period and the criteria set forth by the relevant financial taxonomy standards being used."
