      "problem": "Which delegated regulations define the reporting requirements for environmental objectives under the EU Taxonomy?",
      "solution": "Del. Regulation (EU) 2022/1214, Del. Regulation (EU) 2023/2485, Del. Regulation (EU) 2023/2486, Del. VO (EU) 2021/2139",
      "attempt": "The reporting requirements for environmental objectives under the EU Taxonomy Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2020/852) are primarily defined through delegated acts and regulatory technical standards developed by the European Commission in consultation with the European Supervisory Authorities (ESAs). Specifically, the delegated regulation that plays a key role in defining these requirements is:\n\n- **Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2178**: This regulation complements the Taxonomy Regulation by providing detailed rules on how economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable according to the criteria set out in the Taxonomy Regulation. It includes provisions related to the reporting of information necessary to demonstrate compliance with the taxonomy criteria.\n\nHowever, it's important to note that the actual reporting requirements for companies are further specified in other documents such as:\n\n- **Regulatory Technical Standards (RTS)**: These are developed by ESAs and adopted by the European Commission to provide more detailed guidance on how to apply the Taxonomy Regulation. The RTS cover aspects like methodologies for determining whether an economic activity qualifies as environmentally sustainable and the disclosure requirements for financial market participants and financial advisers.\n\nFor precise and up-to-date information, it would be advisable to consult the official publications from the European Commission and the relevant ESAs, as well as any updates or amendments that may have been issued since the initial publication of these regulations."
