      "solution": "climate change mitigation, pollution prevention and control, protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems, sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources, transition to a circular economy",
      "attempt": "The TRATON GROUP, which includes well-known brands like MAN Truck & Bus and Scania, reports on several environmental objectives under the EU Taxonomy for sustainable activities. For the fiscal year 2023, these objectives typically align with the criteria set out in the EU Taxonomy Regulation, aiming to support climate change mitigation and adaptation. Specifically, the TRATON GROUP focuses on:\n\n1. **Climate Change Mitigation**: This is a primary objective for the TRATON GROUP, as it aims to reduce greenhouse gas emissions from its vehicles and operations. The company works towards developing more efficient and environmentally friendly trucks and buses, as well as supporting the transition to alternative fuels and electrification.\n\n2. **Sustainable Use and Protection of Water and Marine Resources**: While not always the main focus, the TRATON GROUP also considers the sustainable use of water resources in its manufacturing processes and supply chain management.\n\n3. **Waste Prevention and Recycling**: The group aims to minimize waste generation and promote recycling within its operations and product lifecycle.\n\n4. **Pollution Prevention and Control**: Efforts are made to reduce pollution from its products and operations, including air, water, and soil pollution.\n\n5. **Protection and Restoration of Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services**: Although less emphasized compared to climate change mitigation, the TRATON GROUP also takes steps to protect biodiversity and ecosystem services, particularly in areas where its operations have a direct impact.\n\nIt's important to note that the specific details and metrics related to these objectives would be detailed in the TRATON GROUP’s sustainability report or annual financial filings. To get the most accurate and up-to-date information, you should refer to the official TRATON GROUP publications or their website."
