      "attempt": "The EU Taxonomy Regulation outlines six specific environmental objectives that economic activities must substantially contribute to in order to be considered environmentally sustainable. These objectives are:\n\n1. **Climate Change Mitigation**: Activities that significantly reduce greenhouse gas emissions.\n2. **Climate Change Adaptation**: Activities that help build resilience against the impacts of climate change.\n3. **Sustainable Use and Protection of Water and Marine Resources**: Activities that promote the efficient use of water resources and protect marine ecosystems.\n4. **Transition to a Circular Economy**: Activities that support the transition towards a circular economy, including waste prevention, re-use, recycling, and other forms of recovery.\n5. **Pollution Prevention and Control**: Activities that prevent or minimize pollution across various media (air, water, soil).\n6. **Protection and Restoration of Biodiversity and Ecosystems**: Activities that contribute to the protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems.\n\nThese objectives form the core criteria for assessing whether an economic activity can be deemed environmentally sustainable under the EU Taxonomy Regulation."
