      "problem": "Which environmental objectives outlined in the Delegated Acts were assessed by the WashTec Group in relation to EU Taxonomy compliance?",
      "solution": "Pollution prevention and control, Protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems, Sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources, Transition to a circular economy, climate change adaptation, climate change mitigation",
      "attempt": "The WashTec Group, which is a consortium of European washing technology companies, has been involved in assessing the alignment of their industry with the EU Taxonomy for Sustainable Activities. The EU Taxonomy Regulation provides a classification system that aims to help investors identify environmentally sustainable economic activities. It sets out six environmental objectives that economic activities must contribute to in a substantial manner to be considered environmentally sustainable:\n\n1. Climate change mitigation.\n2. Climate change adaptation.\n3. Sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources.\n4. Transition to a circular economy.\n5. Pollution prevention and control.\n6. Protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems.\n\nIn the context of the WashTec Group's assessment, they would likely focus on how their activities align with these objectives, particularly those related to resource efficiency, waste reduction, and pollution control, as these are key areas for washing technologies. However, specific details about which objectives were prioritized or assessed by the WashTec Group would depend on their particular analysis and reports. For precise information, one would need to refer to the detailed assessments or reports produced by the WashTec Group regarding their EU Taxonomy compliance efforts."
