      "question": "Which delegated regulations are referenced in relation to amendments and technical screening criteria under the EU Taxonomy framework?",
      "answer": "Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2139, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2485, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2486",
      "type": "Factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "train:006116:qa_pairs_factoid:0002",
      "difficulty_id": "F-000013",
      "id": "train:006116:qa_pairs_factoid:0002",
      "problem": "Which delegated regulations are referenced in relation to amendments and technical screening criteria under the EU Taxonomy framework?",
      "solution": "Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2139, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2485, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2486",
      "attempt": "The EU Taxonomy Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2020/852) is the primary piece of legislation that establishes the framework for determining which economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable. Under this regulation, the European Commission has the power to adopt delegated acts to specify certain aspects of the taxonomy, including the detailed technical screening criteria for each environmental objective.\n\nSpecifically, the following delegated regulations have been adopted or are in the process of being developed:\n\n1. **Delegated Act on Technical Screening Criteria for Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation**: This act provides detailed criteria for assessing whether an economic activity contributes substantially to climate change mitigation and adaptation objectives. It was adopted in June 2021 and entered into force in July 2021.\n\n2. **Delegated Act on Technical Screening Criteria for Sustainable Use and Protection of Water and Marine Resources**: This act sets out the criteria for assessing activities related to water and marine resources. It was adopted in December 2021 and entered into force in January 2022.\n\n3. **Delegated Act on Technical Screening Criteria for Transition Activities**: This act covers activities that contribute to the transition towards environmentally sustainable economic activities. It was adopted in December 2021 and entered into force in January 2022.\n\n4. **Delegated Act on Technical Screening Criteria for Pollution Prevention and Control**: This act provides criteria for assessing activities related to pollution prevention and control. It was adopted in December 2021 and entered into force in January 2022.\n\n5. **Delegated Act on Technical Screening Criteria for Biodiversity**: This act sets out the criteria for assessing activities that contribute to the protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems. It was adopted in December 2022 and entered into force in January 2023.\n\nThese delegated acts are crucial as they provide the detailed guidance necessary for companies and financial market participants to align their activities with the EU Taxonomy's sustainability objectives. They also serve as the basis for further regulatory developments and policy implementation within the EU."
    },
    {
      "category": "EU Taxonomy",
