      "question": "What are the environmental objectives defined by the EU Taxonomy that guide sustainable economic activities?",
      "answer": "circular economy (CE), climate change adaptation (CCA), climate change mitigation (CCM), pollution prevention and control (PPC), water and marine resources (WTR)",
      "type": "Factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "test:000786:qa_pairs_factoid:0006",
      "difficulty_id": "F-000015",
      "id": "test:000786:qa_pairs_factoid:0006",
      "problem": "What are the environmental objectives defined by the EU Taxonomy that guide sustainable economic activities?",
      "solution": "circular economy (CE), climate change adaptation (CCA), climate change mitigation (CCM), pollution prevention and control (PPC), water and marine resources (WTR)",
      "attempt": "The EU Taxonomy is a classification system designed to provide a common language and framework for investors, companies, and policymakers to understand which economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable. It defines six key environmental objectives that guide sustainable economic activities:\n\n1. **Climate Change Mitigation**: Activities that contribute to reducing greenhouse gas emissions or increasing carbon sequestration.\n\n2. **Climate Change Adaptation**: Actions that help build resilience against the impacts of climate change, such as extreme weather events.\n\n3. **Sustainable Use and Protection of Water and Marine Resources**: Activities that promote the efficient use of water resources and protect marine ecosystems from pollution and degradation.\n\n4. **Transition to a Circular Economy**: Initiatives that support the transition towards a circular economy, including waste prevention, re-use, recycling, and other forms of resource efficiency.\n\n5. **Pollution Prevention and Control**: Measures aimed at preventing or reducing pollution in air, water, and soil, thereby protecting human health and biodiversity.\n\n6. **Protection and Restoration of Biodiversity and Ecosystems**: Efforts to preserve and restore natural habitats and biodiversity, contributing to the long-term health of ecosystems.\n\nEach of these objectives has specific criteria and thresholds that must be met for an activity to be classified as environmentally sustainable under the EU Taxonomy. These criteria ensure that the activities not only contribute positively to the environment but also do no significant harm to any of the other five objectives. This comprehensive approach aims to foster a green economy while ensuring that all aspects of environmental sustainability are considered."
    },
