      "problem": "What sustainability-related financial indicators are disclosed by ATOSS Software AG under the EU Taxonomy framework?",
      "solution": "Group revenue, capital expenditure (Capex), operating expenses (Opex)",
      "attempt": "ATOSS Software AG, as a German company, may be required to disclose certain sustainability-related financial indicators if it falls within the scope of the EU Taxonomy Regulation. The EU Taxonomy is a classification system that aims to provide a common language and framework for companies to report on their environmentally sustainable economic activities.\n\nHowever, as of my last update in October 2023, specific details about what ATOSS Software AG discloses under the EU Taxonomy framework might not be widely publicized or easily accessible without reviewing their latest sustainability reports or annual financial statements. Generally, companies that fall under the EU Taxonomy would need to disclose information related to:\n\n1. **Environmental Objectives**: This includes disclosures on how their activities contribute to any of the six environmental objectives outlined in the taxonomy: climate change mitigation, climate change adaptation, sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources, transition to a circular economy, pollution prevention and control, and protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems.\n\n2. **Do No Significant Harm (DNSH)**: Companies must also ensure that their activities do not cause significant harm to any of the other five environmental objectives if they are primarily aligned with one objective.\n\n3. **Sustainability-Related Financial Disclosures**: These include quantitative and qualitative data on the environmental performance of the company's activities, such as energy consumption, greenhouse gas emissions, and resource efficiency.\n\n4. **Alignment with the EU Taxonomy**: Companies need to disclose the proportion of their turnover, capital expenditure, and operating expenditure that is aligned with the EU Taxonomy.\n\nTo get precise and up-to-date information on what ATOSS Software AG specifically discloses, you should refer to their official sustainability reports, annual financial statements, or contact their investor relations department directly. They will have the most accurate and detailed information regarding their compliance with the EU Taxonomy and related sustainability disclosures."
