      "question": "What categories of investments are eligible under Annex I of IR 2021/2139 for improving energy efficiency?",
      "answer": "Installation, maintenance and repair of energy efficiency equipment, energy-efficient heating concept, investment in energy-saving LED lighting",
      "type": "Factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "test:000745:qa_pairs_factoid:0002",
      "difficulty_id": "F-000016",
      "id": "test:000745:qa_pairs_factoid:0002",
      "problem": "What categories of investments are eligible under Annex I of IR 2021/2139 for improving energy efficiency?",
      "solution": "Installation, maintenance and repair of energy efficiency equipment, energy-efficient heating concept, investment in energy-saving LED lighting",
      "attempt": "Annex I of the Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2139, which is part of the Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR), provides a list of economic activities that can be considered environmentally sustainable. The regulation aims to provide clarity on what constitutes an environmentally sustainable investment and helps investors identify opportunities that contribute positively to environmental sustainability.\n\nUnder this framework, investments aimed at improving energy efficiency fall into several categories. These include, but are not limited to:\n\n1. **Renewable Energy Generation**: Investments in technologies and infrastructure that generate electricity from renewable sources such as solar, wind, hydroelectric, geothermal, and biomass.\n\n2. **Energy Efficiency in Buildings**: This includes improvements in building design, construction, renovation, and operation to reduce energy consumption. Examples might include better insulation, more efficient heating and cooling systems, and the use of smart technology to manage energy usage.\n\n3. **Industrial Energy Efficiency**: Investments in processes, machinery, and equipment that reduce energy consumption in manufacturing and industrial settings. This could involve upgrading to more efficient motors, implementing waste heat recovery systems, or adopting advanced process control technologies.\n\n4. **Transportation Energy Efficiency**: Improvements in transportation systems and vehicles to enhance fuel efficiency and reduce emissions. This could encompass electric vehicles, public transport systems, and logistics optimization.\n\n5. **Energy Storage Solutions**: Investments in technologies that store energy generated from renewable sources, making it available when needed. This includes batteries, pumped hydro storage, and other innovative storage solutions.\n\n6. **Smart Grids and Distribution Networks**: Enhancements to electrical grids to improve their efficiency and reliability, allowing for better integration of renewable energy sources and more effective management of energy demand.\n\n7. **Research and Development in Energy Efficiency Technologies**: Funding for R&D projects aimed at developing new technologies and methods to further improve energy efficiency across various sectors.\n\nEach of these categories represents an area where investments can significantly contribute to improving energy efficiency and reducing overall energy consumption, thereby contributing to environmental sustainability goals. Investors looking to align their portfolios with sustainable finance principles would do well to consider these areas as potential investment opportunities."
    },
