      "id": "test:000751:qa_pairs_factoid:0001",
      "problem": "Which articles define taxonomy-eligible and taxonomy-aligned economic activities in the EU Taxonomy framework?",
      "solution": "Art. 1, nos. 5 and 6, Art. 17 of the Taxonomy Regulation, Art. 8 Delegated Act",
      "attempt": "The definition of taxonomy-eligible and taxonomy-aligned economic activities within the EU Taxonomy framework is primarily outlined in the Delegated Acts adopted under the EU Taxonomy Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2020/852). Specifically, these definitions can be found in:\n\n1. **Delegated Act (EU) 2021/376**: This act sets out the technical screening criteria for climate change mitigation. It defines which economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable in terms of contributing to climate change mitigation.\n\n2. **Delegated Act (EU) 2021/2178**: This act provides the technical screening criteria for climate change adaptation. Similar to the first delegated act, it outlines the conditions for economic activities to be deemed as contributing to climate change adaptation.\n\n3. **Delegated Act (EU) 2022/852**: This act covers the technical screening criteria for sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources, transition to a circular economy, pollution prevention and control, and the protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems. These criteria help determine which economic activities align with each of these environmental objectives.\n\nThese Delegated Acts provide detailed criteria that an economic activity must meet to be considered taxonomy-eligible and taxonomy-aligned. They include specific performance indicators, thresholds, and other requirements that companies must adhere to in order to claim that their activities contribute substantially to one or more of the six environmental objectives outlined in the EU Taxonomy Regulation."
