      "problem": "Which EU Commission communications provide guidance on the interpretation of Article 8 of the Taxonomy Regulation?",
      "solution": "2022/C 385/01, C/2023/305, FAQ on the interpretation of Article 8, draft Commission communication of 21 December 2023",
      "attempt": "The European Union's Taxonomy Regulation aims to provide a classification system for environmentally sustainable activities. Article 8 of the Taxonomy Regulation specifically deals with the disclosure requirements for companies to report on how their economic activities align with the taxonomy criteria.\n\nTo date, the European Commission has issued several communications and delegated acts that provide guidance on the interpretation of Article 8 of the Taxonomy Regulation:\n\n1. **Delegated Act (EU) 2021/337**: This act sets out the content, methodology, and presentation of information that companies must disclose under Article 8. It provides detailed guidance on how companies should report on their alignment with the taxonomy criteria and on the sustainability of their activities.\n\n2. **Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2022/1259**: This regulation further clarifies the disclosure requirements for financial market participants and large undertakings as per Article 8. It specifies the format and structure of the disclosures, ensuring consistency across different types of companies.\n\n3. **Communication from the Commission to the European Parliament, the Council, the European Economic and Social Committee and the Committee of the Regions: \"Guidelines on the application of the Delegated Act on the content, methodology and presentation of information to be disclosed in accordance with Article 8 of the Taxonomy Regulation\"** - While not a formal regulation, this communication offers practical guidance and examples to help companies understand and comply with the disclosure requirements set out in the Delegated Act.\n\nThese documents collectively provide comprehensive guidance on how companies should interpret and apply Article 8 of the Taxonomy Regulation in their reporting practices. Companies are encouraged to consult these official documents to ensure compliance with the regulation's requirements."
