      "problem": "Which internationally recognized frameworks are referenced in the Amadeus Fire Group's efforts to align with governance and compliance standards?",
      "solution": "DIN EN ISO/IEC 27001:2017, ISO 27001, ISO 27701, ISO/IEC 27001 standard",
      "attempt": "I don't have specific information about the Amadeus Fire Group's exact alignment with particular governance and compliance standards or which internationally recognized frameworks they reference. However, companies typically align themselves with well-known frameworks such as:\n\n1. **ISO 27001**: This is an international standard for information security management systems (ISMS). It helps organizations manage their information security risks and ensure that sensitive company and customer information is kept secure.\n\n2. **NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF)**: Developed by the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST), this framework provides a policy framework of computer security guidance for how private sector organizations can assess and improve their ability to prevent, detect, and respond to cyber attacks.\n\n3. **COBIT (Control Objectives for Information and Related Technologies)**: COBIT is a set of best practices for the governance and management of enterprise IT. It helps organizations achieve their goals by ensuring that their IT aligns with business needs and delivers value.\n\n4. **PCI DSS (Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard)**: This standard is designed to ensure that all companies that accept, process, store, or transmit credit card information maintain a secure environment.\n\n5. **GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation)**: Although not a framework per se, GDPR is a regulation in EU law on data protection and privacy for all individuals within the European Union and the European Economic Area. Compliance with GDPR is crucial for any organization handling personal data of EU citizens.\n\n6. **SOC Reports (Service Organization Control Reports)**: These reports provide assurance to stakeholders about the controls at a service organization relevant to user entities' internal control over financial reporting.\n\nIf you're looking for specific details regarding Amadeus Fire Group's compliance efforts, it would be best to refer directly to their official documentation or contact them directly for the most accurate and up-to-date information."
