      "question": "Why are human rights, anti-bribery, anti-corruption, taxation, and fair competition essential components of the European Commission's minimum safeguards, and how do they support compliance with the EU Taxonomy's social and governance objectives?",
      "answer": "The topics include human rights (such as labor and consumer rights), anti-bribery, anti-corruption, taxation, and fair competition. These are significant as they ensure ethical business practices and compliance with international standards, promoting sustainability and preventing harm.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "train:006279:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0003",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
