      "question": "Why does the EU Taxonomy require companies to disclose the shares of turnover, CapEx, and OpEx for Taxonomy-eligible and Taxonomy-non-eligible activities, and how does this enhance transparency for the 2023 financial year?",
      "answer": "The disclosure is required to provide transparency regarding the financial contributions of economic activities to environmental objectives. It helps differentiate between Taxonomy-eligible and non-eligible activities, as well as between Taxonomy-aligned and non-aligned activities for the first two environmental objectives.",
