      "question": "Why has the EU Taxonomy Regulation narrowly defined taxonomy-eligible activities related to the production of physical goods, and what implications does this have for industries producing greenhouse gas-intensive products?",
      "answer": "Only 21 taxonomy-eligible activities are related to the production of physical goods because the EU has narrowly defined these activities to focus on the production of highly greenhouse gas-intensive products, such as aluminum, iron/steel, fertilizers, organic basic materials, selected chemicals, and cement.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "validation:000773:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0005",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
