      "question": "Why are long service life and recyclability essential DNSH criteria for circular economy objectives under the EU Taxonomy, and how do they contribute to sustainable manufacturing and energy generation practices?",
      "answer": "Long service life and recyclability are key DNSH criteria for circular economy objectives, as they ensure that components retain monetary value at the end of their lifecycle and support sustainable practices in manufacturing and energy generation technologies.",
