      "question": "Why do the criteria for climate change mitigation under the EU Taxonomy disqualify data centres (Activity 8.1) based on the global warming potential of refrigerants, despite compliance with other regulations?",
      "answer": "The data centres failed to meet the criteria for substantial contribution to climate change mitigation because the global warming potential (GWP) of refrigerants used in their cooling systems exceeded the defined maximum value of 675, despite complying with Regulation (EU) 517/2014 on fluorinated greenhouse gases.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "test:000755:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0002",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
