      "question": "Why is there a significant gap between taxonomy-eligible and taxonomy-aligned sales revenue percentages, and what does this reveal about the challenges of achieving full compliance with EU Taxonomy criteria?",
      "answer": "The context shows that 92.3% of consolidated sales revenue is taxonomy-eligible, meaning it has the potential to meet EU Taxonomy criteria. In contrast, only 11.4% is taxonomy-aligned, indicating it fully meets the criteria and safeguards. This highlights the gap between eligibility and full compliance.",
