      "question": "Why is it important to review and allocate capitalized internal expenses to specific activities in Vonovia's CapEx, and how does this process prevent duplicate counting while ensuring taxonomy alignment?",
      "answer": "Capitalized internal expenses are reviewed for taxonomy alignment and allocated to specific activities (7.2, 7.3, or 7.7) based on the type of investment. This ensures that the expenses are appropriately categorized and aligned with the taxonomy criteria.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "train:006138:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0012",
