      "question": "What criteria must an economic activity meet to be classified as environmentally sustainable under the Taxonomy Regulation, and why are these criteria significant for achieving the EU's climate goals?",
      "answer": "An economic activity is considered environmentally sustainable if it contributes significantly to at least one of the six environmental objectives, avoids significant harm to other objectives, and adheres to minimum social safeguards.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "train:006218:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0005",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
      "question_word_f1": 0.665,
