      "question": "Why is it important for non-financial companies to distinguish between Taxonomy-eligible and Taxonomy-aligned portions of KPIs, and how does this distinction support the goals of the EU Taxonomy?",
      "answer": "The Taxonomy-eligible portion refers to activities that fall within the scope of the EU Taxonomy framework, while the Taxonomy-aligned portion represents activities that meet specific alignment criteria defined by the Taxonomy. Non-financial companies must disclose both portions in their KPIs.",
