      "question": "Why is the solubility of synthetic amorphous silica (SAS) a key factor in assessing its compliance with EU Taxonomy environmental objectives, particularly regarding health and ecological safety?",
      "answer": "The solubility of SAS is significant because it allows the material to be effectively eliminated from the lungs, minimizing environmental and health impacts such as lung overloading or long-term negative effects.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
