      "solution": "Zalando SE was unable to qualify its Taxonomy-eligible Capex as Taxonomy-aligned for 2023 due to a lack of necessary information for full assessment, as its Capex relates only to the purchase of output.",
      "attempt": "Zalando SE, a leading online platform for fashion and lifestyle products in Europe, has been working towards aligning its operations with sustainable practices and green initiatives. However, the specific issue regarding the inability to qualify certain Taxonomy-eligible Capital Expenditures (CapEx) as Taxonomy-aligned for 2023 is not widely detailed in public statements or reports.\n\nThe EU Taxonomy for Sustainable Activities is a classification system that aims to provide a common language and framework for companies to disclose which parts of their activities are environmentally sustainable. For an investment or economic activity to be considered Taxonomy-aligned, it must meet specific environmental objectives and do no significant harm to other environmental objectives.\n\nIf Zalando SE was unable to qualify some of its Taxonomy-eligible CapEx as Taxonomy-aligned, it could be due to several reasons:\n\n1. **Meeting Environmental Performance Criteria**: The projects might not have met the stringent criteria set out by the EU Taxonomy for reducing greenhouse gas emissions or contributing positively to other environmental objectives.\n   \n2. **Documentation and Reporting**: There may have been issues with the documentation and reporting required to prove that the investments met the necessary criteria. This could include lacking sufficient evidence or data to support claims about the sustainability impact of the projects.\n\n3. **Regulatory Changes**: There could have been changes in regulations or interpretations of the Taxonomy that affected how certain types of CapEx were evaluated.\n\n4. **Project Scope**: Some projects might have included elements that did not fully align with the Taxonomy's requirements, even if they had some sustainable components.\n\nFor precise details on why specific CapEx was not qualified, one would need to refer to Zalando SE’s official communications, financial reports, or sustainability reports where such informat