      "attempt": "The countries contributing employee data for an organization's ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) reporting framework can vary widely depending on the specific organization and its global footprint. Typically, multinational corporations with operations in multiple countries will include data from all of these locations in their ESG reports. This includes information about employee demographics, health and safety records, training programs, diversity initiatives, and more.\n\nTo know exactly which countries contribute to a particular organization's ESG reporting framework, you would need to review the specific ESG report or contact the organization directly for detailed information. Each company's report will list the regions and countries where they operate and provide relevant data from those areas."
