      "problem": "Which diverse stakeholder groups are addressed by wienerberger in its ESG communication strategy?",
      "solution": "analysts and banks, business partners, civil-society organizations (NGOs), customers, designers and architects, employees, investors, local authorities, local residents, media, organized interest groups, political decision-makers, real estate developers, regulators, representatives of the public administration, research institutions, suppliers, universities",
      "attempt": "Wienerberger, a leading provider of innovative and sustainable solutions for the building industry, addresses several diverse stakeholder groups in its ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) communication strategy. These groups include:\n\n1. **Customers**: Wienerberger communicates about its commitment to sustainability, innovation, and quality products that meet environmental standards and contribute to healthier living environments.\n\n2. **Employees**: The company focuses on creating a safe and inclusive workplace, promoting diversity and equal opportunities, and ensuring fair labor practices. It also emphasizes employee development and well-being.\n\n3. **Suppliers and Partners**: Wienerberger works closely with its supply chain to ensure ethical business practices, sustainability, and compliance with environmental regulations. It encourages suppliers to adopt sustainable practices and supports local economies.\n\n4. **Investors and Shareholders**: The company provides transparent information on its financial performance, risk management, and long-term strategic goals related to sustainability and corporate governance.\n\n5. **Communities**: Wienerberger engages with local communities where it operates, contributing to social projects and initiatives that promote sustainable urban development and improve quality of life.\n\n6. **Regulatory Bodies and Authorities**: The company adheres to all relevant laws and regulations and actively participates in discussions and initiatives aimed at improving environmental and social standards.\n\n7. **NGOs and Industry Associations**: Wienerberger collaborates with non-governmental organizations and industry associations to advance sustainability goals and share best practices.\n\nBy addressing these diverse stakeholder groups, Wienerberger aims to build trust, foster collaboration, and drive positive change across its value chain and beyond."
