      "question": "Why are 'Neighborhood development and contribution to infrastructure,' 'Fairly priced housing,' 'Homes that meet people's needs and demographic change,' and 'Customer satisfaction and service quality' considered material social issues in the Non-financial Group Declaration?",
      "answer": "The social issues identified as material topics include 'Neighborhood development and contribution to infrastructure,' 'Fairly priced housing,' 'Homes that meet people's needs and demographic change,' and 'Customer satisfaction and service quality.'",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "ESG",
      "question_id": "train:005794:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0001",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
