      "question": "Why does Manz AG’s commitment to providing a minimum of 16 training hours per employee annually demonstrate its adherence to ESG principles, and how does this contribute to workforce sustainability and long-term organizational resilience?",
      "answer": "Manz AG aims to provide a minimum of 16 training hours per employee annually to ensure consistent and meaningful development opportunities. This reflects the company’s commitment to fostering a skilled workforce and supporting employees’ long-term career growth through structured and adequate training measures.",
