      "question": "Why are exceptions made to the standard payout schedule for Performance Bonus and Performance Shares in cases of permanent incapacity, illness, or death, and how do these exceptions align with ESG principles of social responsibility?",
      "answer": "Exceptions to the standard payout schedule are made if the service contract ends early due to permanent incapacity, another illness, or the death of the Executive Board member. In such cases, the target amount is paid out immediately.",
