      "question": "Why is the SMA Group's definition of serious work-related accidents important for ESG reporting, and how does the absence of such accidents in the reporting year reflect the company's commitment to workplace safety?",
      "answer": "A serious work-related accident at the SMA Group is defined as one where the injured employee cannot fully recover within six months or is not expected to regain their prior state of health. No serious work-related accidents were reported in the year.",
