      "question": "Why is there no direct correlation between laboratory animal usage and sales in the pharmaceutical sector, and how does this distinction reflect the company’s ESG compliance with regulatory and ethical standards?",
      "answer": "There is no direct correlation because laboratory animals in the pharmaceutical sector are primarily used in preclinical research to test the efficacy and safety of drugs still in development, rather than being tied to the sales of approved drugs.",
