      "question": "Why is it essential to categorize 'fuel and energy-related activities' separately from Scope 1 and 2 emissions in ESG reporting, and how does this distinction support more accurate sustainability assessments?",
      "answer": "Categorizing these activities separately allows for a more detailed analysis of indirect energy impacts, ensuring that all relevant emissions are considered in ESG evaluations beyond direct operational control.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
