      "question": "Why is the material performance indicator 'Total number of confirmed cases of corruption (in Germany)' critical for ESG governance reporting, and how does it ensure transparency in corporate accountability?",
      "answer": "This indicator is significant because it reflects only fully completed proceedings, ensuring that the reported figures are based on finalized and verified cases. This approach excludes incidents still under investigation or unresolved, maintaining the accuracy of the key figures.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "ESG",
      "question_id": "train:003745:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0004",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
