        "paragraph": "In 2023, the first crop year without the use of neonicotinoids, about 6,000 hectares of beet fields were lost to beet weevil infestation. The losses were partially compensated for by replanting beet on approximately 4,000 hectares. AGRANA is pleased to have started the 2024 crop year with above-average contracted acreage.\nBesides ensuring sound environmental standards, the maintenance of minimum social standards both within a company and in its supply chain - which Germany has already adopted as part of its Supply Chain Due Diligence Act in force nationally since 2023 - is a further upcoming focus of work for the European Commission as well, under the Corporate Sustainability Due Diligence Directive. For this, several cross-segment\nprojects are already underway at AGRANA, which are managed by the Compliance department to ensure adherence to social standards in the supply chain as well",
