      "problem": "What are the key environmental objectives Hapag-Lloyd aims to achieve in its sustainability strategy?",
      "solution": "alternative fuels, alternative propulsion technologies, carbon-neutral maritime transport, decarbonisation, energy transition, reduce our carbon footprint, reduction of emissions",
      "attempt": "Hapag-Lloyd, one of the world's leading liner shipping companies, has set out several key environmental objectives as part of its sustainability strategy. These objectives reflect the company's commitment to reducing its environmental footprint and contributing positively to global sustainability goals. Here are some of the main environmental targets:\n\n1. **Reduction of CO2 Emissions**: One of the primary goals is to significantly reduce carbon dioxide emissions from its fleet. This involves improving fuel efficiency through modernization of vessels, optimizing routes, and adopting cleaner fuels.\n\n2. **Energy Efficiency**: Enhancing energy efficiency across all operations is another critical objective. This includes investing in advanced technologies and operational practices that minimize energy consumption without compromising service quality.\n\n3. **Use of Alternative Fuels**: Hapag-Lloyd is exploring and implementing the use of alternative fuels such as LNG (liquefied natural gas) and methanol, which produce fewer greenhouse gases compared to traditional marine fuels like heavy fuel oil.\n\n4. **Waste Management**: The company aims to improve waste management practices on board ships and at terminals, focusing on recycling and minimizing waste generation.\n\n5. **Water Management**: Ensuring responsible water management, including preventing pollution from ship operations and promoting sustainable water usage in port facilities.\n\n6. **Biodiversity Protection**: Protecting marine biodiversity by avoiding sensitive areas and ensuring compliance with international regulations aimed at preserving marine ecosystems.\n\n7. **Sustainable Supply Chain**: Encouraging suppliers and partners to adopt sustainable practices, thereby creating a more environmentally friendly supply chain.\n\n8. **Transparency and Reporting**: Committing to transparent reporting on environmental performance and progress towards sustainability goals, allowing stakeholders to track improvements and hold the company accountable.\n\nThese objectives are part of a broader strategy that aligns with international agreements and frameworks, such as the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), particularly Goal 13 (Climate Action) and Goal 14 (Life Below Water). By pursuing these goals, Hapag-Lloyd aims not only to reduce its environmental impact but also to lead the way in sustainable maritime transport."
    },
