      "question": "Why is the conversion of gas turbines at Uniper’s Malmö plant to HVO100 considered a significant step in reducing carbon emissions, and what are the broader implications for sustainable energy transitions?",
      "answer": "The conversion of gas turbines at Uniper’s Malmö plant to Hydrogenated Vegetable Oil (HVO100) results in a CO₂ reduction of around 90%, significantly lowering the carbon footprint of the plant while maintaining its operational flexibility.",
