      "question": "Why do purchased goods and services in the upstream value chain contribute the largest share to the company's total carbon footprint, and how does this classification influence sustainability strategies?",
      "answer": "Purchased goods and services, part of Scope 3 emissions, are classified as the largest share of the company's total carbon footprint because they represent significant greenhouse gas emissions within the upstream value chain.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "Sustainability",
      "question_id": "validation:000251:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0008",
