      "question": "Why is it essential for a bank to report on the environmental, social, and economic impacts of its progress towards sustainability targets, and how does this foster stakeholder trust and accountability?",
      "answer": "Reporting on the impact of progress is important to demonstrate the tangible outcomes of the bank's efforts, ensure accountability, and provide stakeholders with insights into how the bank's actions contribute to its sustainability goals.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
