        ],
        "paragraph": "BREEAM is an internationally recognised certification system that assesses the quality of a building in terms of sustainability. The assessment and certification can take place in many different phases of the life cycle of a building, including during the planning, construction, renovation, or operation.\nThe evaluation covers the following categories:\n- Energy\n- Energy\n- Health and well-being\n- · Innovation\n- Land use\n- Materials\n- Pollution\n- · Management\n- Transport\n- $\\bullet$  Waste\n- Water\nThe critical requirements include aspects such as the use of legally planted and harvested timber and the use of asbestos-free materials.\nDepending on the number of points achieved, a project is assigned the following status:\n- · Pass: 30 to 44 per cent\n- · Pass: 30 to 44 per cent\n- · Good: 45 to 54 per cent\n- Very Good: 55 to 69 per cent\n- Excellent: 70 to 84 per cent\n- · Outstanding: over 84 per cent\nLEED-certified properties offer the following benefits:\n- · Improved energy efficiency\n- · Improved energy efficiency\n- Lower CO<sub>2</sub> emissions and lower impact on climate change\n- Lower operating costs\n- Protection of water resources\n- Healthier sites for people\n- $\\bullet$  Closed-loop waste management\nIn order to obtain LEED certification, points are assigned for CO<sub>2</sub> emissions, energy consumption, water, waste, transport, materials, health, and indoor environmental quality.\nDepending on the number of points achieved, a property is assigned the following status:\n- · Certified: 40 to 49 points\n- · Certified: 40 to 49 points\n- · Silver: 50 to 59 points\n- · Gold: 60 to 79 points\n- · Platinum: over 79 points",
