      "question": "Why are the material requirements, such as the use of legally sourced timber and asbestos-free materials, critical for achieving BREEAM certification and ensuring sustainable construction practices?",
      "answer": "Critical material requirements for BREEAM certification include the use of legally planted and harvested timber and asbestos-free materials. These requirements ensure that materials used in construction are sustainable and safe for both the environment and occupants.",
