      "question": "Why is the organization's risk management approach critical for addressing human rights and environmental challenges in the supply chain, and how does it ensure compliance with sustainability goals?",
      "answer": "The risk management approach focuses on identifying and addressing human rights and environmental risks along the supply chain. It involves conducting annual and ad-hoc risk assessments to ensure compliance and mitigate potential issues.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "Sustainability",
      "question_id": "train:002299:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0002",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
