      "question": "Why does Eckert & Ziegler's operational model, including its material processing and sourcing practices, position it as a low emitter of carbon dioxide within the chemical-pharmaceutical industry?",
      "answer": "Eckert & Ziegler considers itself a low emitter of carbon dioxide because it processes relatively small masses in its products, minimizes transport emissions, and sources raw materials from nuclear reactors, which operate without producing carbon dioxide.",
